+ * keeps the first CS_LOG_CAP bytes of its output in /tmp/reaper/script-<name>.log (the last run only) and logs
+ * one line when it exits non-zero, with the last thing it printed. The output goes through a pipe, never
+ * straight to the file: a daemon the script starts keeps its stdout, and through a file it could fill RAM;
+ * past the cap the watcher reads and drops. The caller's contract is stock: timeout 0 returns at once
+ * (the script is not waited for), timeout > 0 waits for the script - not for the watcher, which a daemon
